 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Reset timing",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "When VDD falls through the threshold the reset output goes active, typically 65 µs later. After VDD rises back above the threshold the output stays active for the timeout, 140 ms at least, before releasing."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output types",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Both versions have a push-pull output. The TCM809 asserts its output low (/RESET), the TCM810 high (RESET). The output state is defined for VDD down to 1 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply glitch rejection",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Brief negative dips on VDD are rejected. A dip resets the part only when its depth below VTH (overdrive) and its length together lie above the maximum-transient-duration curve; dips under the curve cause no reset, dips above it count as a brown-out or power-down. A capacitor close to the VDD pin raises the immunity."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Behaviour below VDD = 1.0 V",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Under 1.0 V the TCM809 output goes high-impedance and stops sinking current, so a CMOS reset input driven by it floats. Where reset must hold all the way to 0 V, a pull-down from /RESET to ground (100 kΩ suits most designs) holds the line low; the TCM810 needs a pull-up from RESET to VDD for the same purpose."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Bidirectional reset pins",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Where the microcontroller's reset pin can also drive, a fight between it and the supervisor output can leave the line at an undefined level, depending on how strongly the pin drives. A 4.7 kΩ resistor in series with the supervisor output prevents this. Other devices that need reset take it through a buffer, so that they do not load the line."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ordering code",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "A part number is the device (TCM809 or TCM810), a threshold letter (L 4.63 V, M 4.38 V, J 4.00 V, T 3.08 V, S 2.93 V, R 2.63 V, Z 2.32 V), a temperature letter (E -40 °C to +85 °C, V -40 °C to +125 °C) and a package code (NB713 SOT-23B or LB713 SC-70, both 3-pin on tape and reel)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package marking",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "SOT-23B parts carry a four-character code XXNN: the two-character code of the part-number table and a traceability code. SC-70 parts carry either XXN on top with a year digit and week YWW underneath, or XXNN on top. The packages are Pb-free with matte tin (e3)."
  }
 ],
